      <h2>The Celiac Drive-Thru Ordering Script</h2>
      <p>When ordering a naturally gluten-free Blizzard (such as Butterfinger or Reese's) with medical celiac requirements, use this precise script to trigger proper kitchen procedures:</p>
      
      <div style="background:#F0FDF4;border-left:4px solid #16A34A;padding:18px 22px;border-radius:0 14px 14px 0;margin:20px 0;">
        <p style="margin:0;font-weight:700;color:#14532D;font-size:1.05rem;">The Spindle Sanitization Script:</p>
        <p style="margin:6px 0 0 0;font-style:italic;color:#166534;">"Hi, I have a medical allergy to gluten. Could you please wash your hands, change gloves, and use a fresh sanitized spindle collar and blade before blending my Butterfinger Blizzard?"</p>
        <p style="margin:8px 0 0 0;color:#14532D;font-size:0.9rem;">Crew members are trained to execute this sanitization protocol upon request at all corporate-compliant franchises.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Hot Food Allergen Guide: Burgers &amp; Savory Bites</h2>
      <p>Dining on savory foods from <a href="/categories/burgers-sandwiches">The Queen Dairy Burger Lineup</a> requires specific adjustments:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>100% Pure Beef Patties:</strong> DQ beef patties contain no wheat binders or gluten fillers. Always request your burger <em>"protein-style in a lettuce wrap or plastic bowl"</em> to avoid the bun.</li>
        <li><strong>Avoid Texas Toast &amp; Breaded Strips:</strong> The garlic Texas toast and crispy chicken tenderloins contain heavy wheat flour coatings.</li>
        <li><strong>Condiment Safety:</strong> Standard ketchup, yellow mustard, and FlameThrower sauce do not contain gluten ingredients. Barbecue sauces should be verified individually as recipes can rotate seasonally.</li>
      </ul>

